#Model tuning 
->model tuning means adjusting the settings of a ml model to get better performance. This settings are called hyperparameters.

=>why do we tune a model
->Underfit = Model is too simple and performs poorly
->Overfit = Model learns the training data too closely and performs poorly on new data
->Good fit = model performs well on both training and unseen data

=>Common tuning methods 
->grid search
->Random Search
->Cross Validation
